{"id":"W2052218930","title":"The Pen Is Mightier Than the Keyboard: Advantages of Longhand Over Laptop Note Taking","year":2014,"abstract":"Three experiments examined whether taking notes by hand versus on a laptop affects learning. In the first two experiments, participants took notes on lectures and were tested on factual and conceptual questions. Longhand note takers performed better than laptop note takers on conceptual questions, even though laptop note takers recorded more content. A third experiment found that laptop note takers tended to transcribe lectures verbatim, and this tendency was associated with poorer learning. The studies did not include a note-review manipulation."}
